<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> This is historically our toughest matchup.
    Full English Breakfast / Devourer is a redundant, blazingly fast graveyard
    combo: it uses <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Survival of the Fittest"
        >Survival of the Fittest</a
    > to assemble <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Sutured Ghoul">Sutured Ghoul</a
    > powered by <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Phyrexian Devourer"
        >Phyrexian Devourer</a
    > and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Dragon Breath">Dragon Breath</a
    >. Their goldfish clock is faster than our interaction and shrugs off most
    standard disruption.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Cut every <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
    > and trim spot removal like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >—it doesn't touch their engine. Load up on cheap answers instead: <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    > (name Survival or whatever their main reanimation piece is), <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Arcane Denial">Arcane Denial</a
    >, and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Hydroblast">Hydroblast</a
    > if they lean on red discard or looting.
</p>
